      "message": "Equivalent of how that property behaves *for Java*. It does nothing for the NDK. How about:\n\n```\nThe API level that this module is built against. The APIs of this API level will be visible at build time, but use of any APIs newer than min_sdk_version will render the module unloadable on older devices. In the future it will be possible to weakly-link new APIs, making the behavior match Java: such modules will load on older devices, but calling new APIs on devices that do not support them will result in a crash.\n\nThis property has the same behavior as sdk_version does for Java modules. For those familiar with Android Gradle, the property behaves similarly to how compileSdkVersion does for Java code.\n```",
